  "notes": "Modified cash basis village, FYE 9/30/22. Governmental lines from the governmental funds statement p5 Total column; Loan proceeds 361,048 and Sale of equipment 2,505 are printed inside Total revenues, so recorded as receipt lines. Contributions and grants 115,173 kept as one line (General 89,244 = Contributions 87,848 + Grant income 1,396 on p10; Street 25,929 has no printed breakdown). Capital outlay 288,053 is entirely in the Street Fund column -> Capital Outlay: Streets/Highways. Governmental cash: only the 9/30/22 balance sheet is printed (cash and cash equivalents 364,291 plus county treasurer cash 5,353, p4); no beginning cash printed, so the roll-forward uses fund balances (489,238 + 886,635 - 776,229 + 29,990 - 259,990 = 369,644). Transfers summed from fund columns (in: Street 29,990; out: General 221,600 + CDA 29,990 + Keno 8,400; Total column prints net (230,000)); business-type Water +230,000. Business-type (Water, Sewer, Trash) from p7 by cost type plus principal/interest/fees; disbursements total 169,778 printed on p2 (operating 101,272 + nonoperating 68,506); cash measure (-73,656 -> 145,046). Proprietary cash flow statement p8 printed but left null as in FY2024. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds Balance Sheet p4 (totals equal the government-wide 369,644), business-type from p1. Detail: General Fund departments schedule p10 by department column; the p9 all-funds budget schedule's governmental lines combine all funds so are not recorded; its Water/Sewer/Trash expenditure lines recorded with budget. Street, Community Development Agency and Keno funds have no schedule of their own. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
